# November 28, 2026: Carnegie libraries of Oregon: a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings Andrew
# Carnegie paid for on the map. Baker City's Carnegie library (the Crossroads Carnegie Art Center) was already on the Atlas
# and is not added again; Portland's Central Library, already there, was not a Carnegie building.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's list of Carnegie libraries in Oregon and its articles; the Oregon Encyclopedia;
# National Register records and nominations (the Park Service, and the state's copy of La Grande's); the libraries', museums',
# arts centers' and cities' own pages; Newberg Public Library's 2012 Carnegie passport; the East Oregonian; Waymarking;
# HMdb; the University of Oregon's Building Oregon photographs; a history of the Josephine County library; a 2012 blog
# visit to McMinnville.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses and street corners, OpenStreetMap points for named buildings; not yet
# looked at on the aerial.
